        }
      ],
      "callouts": [
        {
          "type": "common_error",
          "text_md": "**No digas:** *I didn't went.* **Di:** *I didn't go.* Después de *didn't*, el verbo siempre va en forma base, nunca en pasado."
        },
        {
          "type": "warning",
          "text_md": "**Cuidado con *be*:** No uses *didn't* con *was/were*. Para *be* en negativo, usa *wasn't* (singular) o *weren't* (plural). Ejemplo: *She wasn't unhappy.*"
        },
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "text_md": "**Recuerda:** *Didn't* es igual para todas las personas. No necesitas cambiar nada: *I didn't*, *he didn't*, *they didn't*."
        }
      ],
      "common_errors_es": [
        "Usar el verbo en pasado después de didn't: *I didn't went* → *I didn't go*.",
        "Usar didn't con was/were: *I didn't was scared* → *I wasn't scared*.",
        "Olvidar el verbo en forma base: *She didn't appeared* → *She didn't appear*."
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "past simple: questions with did",
      "title_form": "Preguntas en pasado con did",
      "title_target": "Past simple questions with did",
      "description_md_form": "Para hacer **preguntas** sobre el pasado, usamos el auxiliar **did** + el verbo en **forma base**. El verbo principal NO cambia a pasado; solo `did` lleva la marca de pasado.\n\n**Estructura:** `Did + sujeto + verbo (base) + ...?`\n\n- `Did you see the cat?` = ¿Viste al gato?\n- `Did she feel scared?` = ¿Ella se sintió asustada?\n\n**Respuestas cortas:**\n- Sí: `Yes, I did.` / `Yes, she did.`\n- No: `No, I didn't.` / `No, she didn't.`\n\n**Importante:** `did` es igual para todas las personas (I, you, he, she, it, we, they). No decimos `Did you saw...`, sino `Did you see...`.",
      "description_md_target": "To make **questions** about the past, we use the auxiliary **did** + the verb in **base form**. The main verb does NOT change to past; only `did` carries the past marker.\n\n**Structure:** `Did + subject + verb (base) + ...?`\n\n- `Did you see the cat?`\n- `Did she feel scared?`\n\n**Short answers:**\n- Yes: `Yes, I did.` / `Yes, she did.`\n- No: `No, I didn't.` / `No, she didn't.`\n\n**Important:** `did` is the same for all persons (I, you, he, she, it, we, they). We don't say `Did you saw...`, we say `Did you see...`.",
      "grammar_structure": "Did + subject + verb (base form) + ...?",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "past_simple_questions",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Pregunta",
          "Respuesta corta sí",
          "Respuesta corta no"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "Did I appear...?",
            "Yes, I did.",
            "No, I didn't."
          ],
          [
            "you",
            "Did you appear...?",
            "Yes, you did.",
            "No, you didn't."
          ],
          [
            "he/she/it",
            "Did she appear...?",
            "Yes, she did.",
            "No, she didn't."
          ],
          [
            "we",
            "Did we appear...?",
            "Yes, we did.",
            "No, we didn't."
          ],
          [
            "they",
            "Did they appear...?",
            "Yes, they did.",
            "No, they didn't."
          ]
        ]
      },
